                                |\n                        +-----------------+-----------------+\n                        | External Integration Adapters     |\n                        +-----------------+-----------------+\n                                          |\n           +------------------------------+------------------------------+\n           |                              |                              |\n           v                              v                              v\n     [LLM Providers]                [Stripe API]              [Google & Email]\n  - OpenAI / Gemini               - Checkout Sessions       - Google Calendar v3\n  - Standard Mock Adapter         - Webhooks (HMAC SHA256)  - Nodemailer / SMTP\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Module Boundaries & Design Rationale\n\n1. **Auth & User (`/modules/auth`, `/modules/users`)**: Encapsulates credential management and profiles. Passwords are never returned in queries.\n2. **AI Chat (`/modules/chat`)**: Manages session metadata and message threads. LLM calls run server-side only; keys are never sent to the browser.\n3. **Resumes (`/modules/resumes`)**: Stores raw data in structured JSON schemas rather than unstructured HTML. This allows lossless template switching.\n4. **Consultants & Bookings (`/modules/consultants`, `/modules/bookings`)**: Implements strict overlapping verification and past-date rejection.\n5. **Payments (`/modules/payments`)**: Adheres to strict server-side pricing. The client cannot forge or alter the checkout price.\n6. **External Integrations (`/integrations`)**: Abstracted via adapters (`llm.ts`, `calendar.ts`, `email.ts`). If external API credentials are not provided, built-in development fallback adapters maintain zero-friction local functionality.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Database Schema Overview\n\n- **User**: Name, unique lowercase email, bcrypt password hash, role (`USER`, `ADMIN`, `CONSULTANT`), embedded profile (headline, bio, skills, education, experience, projects).\n- **ChatSession**: User reference, title, timestamps, compound index on `{ userId: 1, updatedAt: -1 }`.\n- **ChatMessage**: Session reference, user reference, role (`user`, `assistant`, `system`), content, indexed by session and creation time.\n- **Resume**: User reference, title, template (`MODERN_PROFESSIONAL` or `ATS_CLASSIC`), structured personal info, summary, experience, education, skills, projects, certifications, achievements.\n- **Consultant**: Name, title, bio, expertise array, hourly rate (cents), session duration, availability array (day of week, start/end time), active status.\n- **Booking**: User reference, consultant reference, agenda, start time, end time, duration, server-calculated amount, status state machine (`PENDING_PAYMENT`, `PAYMENT_FAILED`, `PAID`, `CONFIRMED`, `CANCELLED`, `COMPLETED`), calendar & email integration status.\n- **Payment**: Booking reference (unique), user reference, Stripe session ID (unique), payment intent ID, amount, currency, status (`PENDING`, `SUCCEEDED`, `FAILED`), processed webhook events array (for strict idempotency).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Authentication Strategy\n\n- **Tokens**: JSON Web Tokens (JWT) signed with HMAC SHA-256.\n- **Cookie Security**: Issued in `HTTP-Only`, `SameSite: Lax`, and `Secure` (in production) cookies to prevent XSS credential theft.\n- **Authorization Header**: Bearer token is supported as a fallback for API clients and automated tests.\n- **Access Isolation**: Every database query filters by `userId: req.user.userId`. Cross-user data access is rejected with `HTTP 403 Forbidden`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. AI Resume Generation & Templates\n\n### Two Production Templates:\n1. **Modern Professional**: Modern typography (Inter), clear visual hierarchy, balanced whitespace, modern header, clean badge styling.\n2. **ATS Classic**: Traditional serif typography (Times New Roman), standardized single-column layout, semantic heading hierarchy, machine-readable formatting designed for applicant tracking systems.\n\nBoth templates consume the same underlying JSON data model. Switching templates in the editor or preview changes only presentation; no resume fields are lost or duplicated.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Stripe Payment Workflow & Webhook Idempotency\n\n1. User selects an open slot for an expert.\n2. Backend checks availability, calculates the price, and creates a `PENDING_PAYMENT` booking.\n3. User initiates checkout -> backend creates a Stripe Checkout Session with line items calculated strictly from the database.\n4. User completes payment on Stripe.\n5. Stripe sends `checkout.session.completed` webhook to `/api/payments/webhook`.\n6. Backend verifies the raw HMAC signature using `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent()`.\n7. **Idempotency check**: The backend inspects `Payment.processedWebhookEvents`. If the event ID was already recorded, the handler responds immediately with HTTP 200 without duplicate action.\n8. Transition booking to `CONFIRMED` and payment to `SUCCEEDED`.\n9. Trigger Google Calendar and Email invitations. If either fails, the booking remains confirmed and the error is logged without failing the payment.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Environment Variables\n\nCreate a `.env` file in the project root or backend folder:\n\n```env\n# Server\nNODE_ENV=development\nPORT=5000\nFRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000\nBACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5000\n\n# Database\nMONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/career_platform\n\n# Security\nJWT_SECRET=super-secret-jwt-key-min-32-chars-long-for-production-security\nJWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d\nCOOKIE_SECRET=super-secret-cookie-secret-key-32-chars-long\n\n# AI Provider ('mock', 'openai', 'gemini')\nLLM_PROVIDER=mock\nLLM_API_KEY=\nLLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini\n\n# Stripe Payments\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_placeholder_key\nSTRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_placeholder_webhook_secret\nNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_placeholder_publishable_key\n\n# Google Calendar (optional, uses MockAdapter if empty)\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=\nGOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5000/api/calendar/callback\nGOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=\n\n# Email SMTP (optional, uses MockAdapter if empty)\nEMAIL_HOST=smtp.mailtrap.io\nEMAIL_PORT=587\nEMAIL_USER=\nEMAIL_PASSWORD=\nEMAIL_FROM=no-reply@careerplatform.com\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Local Setup & Startup Instructions\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Node.js v20+ or v22+\n- npm v10+\n- MongoDB (local `mongod` or Docker container)\n\n### 1. Start MongoDB\nUsing the installed MongoDB server:\n```powershell\nmongod --dbpath ./data/db\n```\nOr via Docker:\n```bash\ndocker compose up -d mongodb\n```\n\n### 2. Backend Setup & Run\n```bash\ncd backend\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\nBackend will start on `http://localhost:5000`.\n- Swagger API Docs: `http://localhost:5000/api/docs`\n- Health check: `http://localhost:5000/health`\n\n### 3. Frontend Setup & Run\n```bash\ncd frontend\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\nFrontend will be accessible at `http://localhost:3000`.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Automated Testing\n\nAll 5 core suites run against an isolated in-memory MongoDB instance:\n\n```bash\ncd backend\nnpm test\n```\n\n### Test Coverage Summary:\n- **Authentication**: Registration, duplicate email rejection, password checks, HTTP-only cookie issuance, profile update.\n- **Resumes**: CRUD, user access isolation, template switching, AI generation, semantic export.\n- **AI Chat Assistant**: Multi-turn message exchange, history retention, session rename, deletion, access isolation.\n- **Consultation Booking**: Past booking rejection, slot reservation, concurrency conflict (double-booking) rejection, server-side pagination, search, and filtering.\n- **Stripe Payments**: Server pricing, webhook processing, state transition to `CONFIRMED`, webhook idempotency, integration failure isolation.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Production Build\n\nBuild backend:\n```bash\ncd backend\nnpm run build\n```\n\nBuild frontend:\n```bash\ncd frontend\nnpm run build\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. Scaling Considerations for 1 Million Users\n\n1. **Stateless Backend**: Express APIs are stateless; horizontal autoscaling behind AWS ALB or Cloudflare.\n2. **MongoDB Sharding**: Shard `chatmessages` by `{ sessionId: 1 }` and `resumes` by `{ userId: 1 }`.\n3. **Read Replicas**: Route dashboard queries and consultant availability searches to secondary replicas.\n4. **Redis Cache Layer**: Cache consultant availability slots and public consultant directory with TTL invalidation.\n5. **Durable Message Queues**: Queue Stripe webhook jobs and email/calendar dispatches via RabbitMQ or AWS SQS.\n","Description":"Create comprehensive README.md documentation","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\README.md","toolAction":"Writing README.md","toolSummary":"Create README.md"}}]}
