{"step_index":286,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:24:15Z","content":"# AI-Powered Career and Consultation Platform\n\nThe **CareerOS Platform** has been fully implemented, tested, and built. It is a complete, production-oriented full-stack web application with Next.js 14 App Router on the frontend, Express.js with TypeScript and Mongoose on the backend, persistent MongoDB database schemas, LLM integration, Stripe Checkout with webhook idempotency, Google Calendar synchronization, automated email confirmations, and automated test coverage.\n\nThe project is located at:\n`C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform`\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> It is recommended to set `C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform` as your active workspace directory in your editor or terminal.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Summary of Implemented Features\n\n### 1. Authentication & User Profile Management\n- Secure user registration and login with bcrypt password hashing.\n- Token-based authentication using JSON Web Tokens (JWT) issued in **HTTP-Only cookies** (`token`) with Bearer header fallback.\n- Role-based authorization (`USER`, `ADMIN`, `CONSULTANT`).\n- Comprehensive profile management: Headline, biography, contact info, skills, education, work experience, projects, and certifications.\n- Protected frontend routes and backend APIs with resource ownership verification.\n\n### 2. AI Career Assistant (ChatGPT-Style Coach)\n- Persistent multi-turn conversations stored in MongoDB ([`ChatSession`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/modules/chat/chat.model.ts) and [`ChatMessage`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/modules/chat/chat.model.ts)).\n- Real-time conversation context preservation (STAR interview method, salary negotiation strategies, system design coaching).\n- Session management: Create new chats, rename sessions with inline modals, switch between threads, and delete sessions.\n- Pluggable AI provider abstraction ([`llm.ts`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/integrations/llm.ts)) supporting OpenAI, Gemini, and a development fallback mock provider.\n\n### 3. AI Resume Builder & Tiptap Rich Text Editor\n- Multi-section structured resume model ([`Resume`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/modules/resumes/resume.model.ts)): Personal info, summary, experience, education, skills, projects, certifications, and achievements.\n- Resume content stored independently of visual presentation (no destructive raw HTML coupling).\n- Interactive **Tiptap rich text editor** ([`TiptapResumeEditor.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/frontend/components/editor/TiptapResumeEditor.tsx)) supporting bold, italics, headers, and bulleted/numbered lists with bidirectional state synchronization.\n- Targeted AI section generation/refinement: Users can trigger AI generation specifically for summary, experience bullets, or skills without altering other fields.\n- Full CRUD operations: Create, list, edit, preview, delete, and export resumes.\n\n### 4. Dual Resume Templates & ATS-Friendly Output\n- **Template A: Modern Professional**: Contemporary typography, clear visual hierarchy, balanced whitespace, and subtle border accents.\n- **Template B: ATS Classic**: Single-column conventional layout, semantic HTML heading hierarchy (`header`, `main`, `section`, `h1`, `h2`, `h3`, `ul`, `li`), and machine-readable text designed for applicant tracking systems.\n- Seamless template switching: Switching templates updates presentation while preserving structured resume data.\n- Export options: One-click browser print / PDF export (`window.print()`) and downloadable raw semantic HTML.\n\n### 5. Consultant Directory & Concurrency-Guarded Booking\n- Consultant directory with real-time slot availability calculation.\n- Seeded demonstration experts: Sarah Jenkins (Staff Recruiter), David Chen (VP of Engineering), and Maya Patel (Design Director).\n- Strict business validation: Rejection of bookings in the past, time-boundary validation, and active slot verification.\n- **Concurrency & Overlapping Safeguards**: Database-level overlapping reservation query prevents double-booking identical or intersecting slots (returns `HTTP 409 Conflict`).\n- Explicit booking state machine: `PENDING_PAYMENT` $\\rightarrow$ `PAID` $\\rightarrow$ `CONFIRMED`, `PAYMENT_FAILED`, `CANCELLED`, `COMPLETED`.\n\n### 6. Stripe Payment Integration & Webhook Idempotency\n- Server-side price calculation: The browser cannot specify or forge consultation fees.\n- Stripe Checkout session creation (`/api/payments/checkout`) with automatic redirects.\n- Webhook signature verification: Cryptographic HMAC SHA256 verification using `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent()`.\n- **Event Ledger Idempotency**: Processed Stripe event IDs (`event.id`) are tracked in [`Payment.processedWebhookEvents`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/modules/payments/payment.model.ts). Re-delivering identical webhook events returns `HTTP 200` without duplicating state transitions or notifications.\n- Verified payment status page (`/payment/success`) validates payment and booking status via backend database verification rather than trusting browser redirects.\n\n### 7. Google Calendar & Email Integrations with Failure Isolation\n- **Google Calendar Adapter** ([`calendar.ts`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/integrations/calendar.ts)): Generates meeting event IDs and Google Meet video links.\n- **Email Adapter** ([`email.ts`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/integrations/email.ts)): Dispatches HTML confirmation emails containing the booking ID, date, time, consultant details, agenda, and video link.\n- **Failure Isolation**: If Google Calendar or Nodemailer encounters third-party outages, the confirmed payment and booking status are preserved; integration errors are flagged on the booking record (`calendarStatus: 'FAILED'`, `emailStatus: 'FAILED'`) for asynchronous retries.\n\n### 8. Analytics Dashboard & Server-Side Pagination\n- User-scoped dashboard aggregation pipeline ([`dashboard.controller.ts`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/modules/dashboard/dashboard.controller.ts)): Total resumes, total chat sessions, upcoming consultations, completed consultations, recent resumes, and upcoming appointments.\n- Server-side pagination, search, sorting whitelist, and status filtering on the consultations listing API ([`booking.controller.ts`](file:///C:/Users/PRIYANKA/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/career-platform/backend/src/modules/bookings/booking.controller.ts)).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Final Folder Structure\n\n```\ncareer-platform/\n├── .env.example\n├── .gitignore\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── README.md\n│\n├── docs/\n│   ├── architecture.md\n│   ├── database-design.md\n│   ├── api-documentation.md\n│   └── testing.md\n│\n├── backend/\n│   ├── package.json\n│   ├── tsconfig.json\n│   ├── jest.config.js\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── config/\n│   │   │   ├── env.ts\n│   │   │   └── database.ts\n│   │   ├── middleware/\n│   │   │   ├── auth.ts\n│   │   │   ├── errorHandler.ts\n│   │   │   └── validate.ts\n│   │   ├── utils/\n│   │   │   ├── errors.ts\n│   │   │   └── logger.ts\n│   │   ├── integrations/\n│   │   │   ├── llm.ts\n│   │   │   ├── calendar.ts\n│   │   │   └── email.ts\n│   │   ├── modules/\n│   │   │   ├── auth/\n│   │   │   │   ├── auth.controller.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── auth.routes.ts\n│   │   │   │   └── auth.validation.ts\n│   │   │   ├── users/\n│   │   │   │   ├── user.model.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── user.controller.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── user.routes.ts\n│   │   │   │   └── user.validation.ts\n│   │   │   ├── chat/\n│   │   │   │   ├── chat.model.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── chat.controller.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── chat.routes.ts\n│   │   │   │   └── chat.validation.ts\n│   │   │   ├── resumes/\n│   │   │   │   ├── resume.model.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── resume.controller.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── resume.routes.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── resume.templates.ts\n│   │   │   │   └── resume.validation.ts\n│   │   │   ├── consultants/\n│   │   │   │   ├── consultant.model.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── consultant.controller.ts\n│   │   │   │   └── consultant.routes.ts\n│   │   │   ├── bookings/\n│   │   │   │   ├── booking.model.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── booking.controller.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── booking.routes.ts\n│   │   │   │   └── booking.validation.ts\n│   │   │   ├── payments/\n│   │   │   │   ├── payment.model.ts\n│   │   │   │   ├── payment.controller.ts\n│   │   │   │   └── payment.routes.ts\n│   │   │   └── dashboard/\n│   │   │       ├── dashboard.controller.ts\n│   │   │       └── dashboard.routes.ts\n│   │   ├── app.ts\n│   │   └── server.ts\n│   └── tests/\n│       ├── setup.ts\n│       ├── auth.test.ts\n│       ├── resumes.test.ts\n│       ├── chat.test.ts\n│       ├── bookings.test.ts\n│       └── payments.test.ts\n│\n└── frontend/\n    ├── package.json\n    ├── tsconfig.json\n    ├── next.config.js\n    ├── tailwind.config.js\n    ├── postcss.config.js\n    ├── types/\n    │   └── index.ts\n    ├── lib/\n    │   ├── api.ts\n    │   └── utils.ts\n    ├── components/\n    │   ├── ui/\n    │   │   ├── Button.tsx\n    │   │   ├── Input.tsx\n    │   │   ├── Card.tsx\n    │   │   ├── Badge.tsx\n    │   │   ├── Skeleton.tsx\n    │   │   └── Modal.tsx\n    │   ├── layout/\n    │   │   ├── Sidebar.tsx\n    │   │   ├── Navbar.tsx\n    │   │   └── DashboardLayout.tsx\n    │   ├── editor/\n    │   │   └── TiptapResumeEditor.tsx\n    │   └── templates/\n    │       └── ResumePreview.tsx\n    └── app/\n        ├── layout.tsx\n        ├── page.tsx\n        ├── globals.css\n        ├── (auth)/\n        │   ├── login/page.tsx\n        │   └── register/page.tsx\n        ├── dashboard/page.tsx\n        ├── profile/page.tsx\n        ├── chat/\n        │   ├── page.tsx\n        │   └── [sessionId]/page.tsx\n        ├── resumes/\n        │   ├── page.tsx\n        │   ├── create/page.tsx\n        │   └── [id]/\n        │       ├── edit/page.tsx\n        │       └── preview/page.tsx\n        ├── consultations/\n        │   ├── page.tsx\n        │   └── book/page.tsx\n        └── payment/\n            ├── success/page.tsx\n            └── cancel/page.tsx\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency Installation Commands\n\nFrom the workspace root:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install Backend Dependencies\ncd C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\backend\nnpm install\n\n# 2. Install Frontend Dependencies\ncd C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\frontend\nnpm install\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Application Startup Commands\n\n### Step 1: Start MongoDB\nEnsure MongoDB is running locally on port 27017:\n```powershell\nmongod --dbpath \"C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\data\\db\"\n```\n*(Or use Docker: `docker compose up -d mongodb`)*\n\n### Step 2: Start the Backend Server (Express + TypeScript)\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\backend\nnpm run dev\n```\n- API Base URL: `http://localhost:5000`\n- Interactive Swagger / OpenAPI Documentation: `http://localhost:5000/api/docs`\n- Health check: `http://localhost:5000/health`\n\n### Step 3: Start the Frontend Application (Next.js 14)\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\frontend\nnpm run dev\n```\n- Access the web application at: `http://localhost:3000`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Environment Variables Configuration\n\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env` in the backend root:\n\n```env\n# Server\nNODE_ENV=development\nPORT=5000\nFRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000\nBACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5000\n\n# Database\nMONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/career_platform\n\n# Security & Authentication\nJWT_SECRET=super-secret-jwt-key-min-32-chars-long-for-production-security\nJWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d\nCOOKIE_SECRET=super-secret-cookie-secret-key-32-chars-long\n\n# AI Provider ('mock' for local dev, 'openai' for production)\nLLM_PROVIDER=mock\nLLM_API_KEY=\nLLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini\n\n# Stripe Payments (Test Mode)\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_placeholder_key\nSTRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_placeholder_webhook_secret\nNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_placeholder_publishable_key\n\n# Google Calendar (Optional - leaves empty to use development MockCalendarAdapter)\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=\nGOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5000/api/calendar/callback\nGOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=\n\n# Email SMTP (Optional - leaves empty to use development MockEmailAdapter)\nEMAIL_HOST=smtp.mailtrap.io\nEMAIL_PORT=587\nEMAIL_USER=\nEMAIL_PASSWORD=\nEMAIL_FROM=no-reply@careerplatform.com\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Third-Party Account Setup Instructions\n\n1. **Stripe Test Mode**:\n   - Create a free account at [stripe.com](https://stripe.com).\n   - In developer mode, obtain your `Secret key` (`sk_test_...`) and `Publishable key` (`pk_test_...`).\n   - For webhooks: Install the Stripe CLI (`stripe listen --forward-to localhost:5000/api/payments/webhook`) and copy the signing secret (`whsec_...`) into `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`.\n2. **OpenAI / LLM Provider**:\n   - Generate an API key at [platform.openai.com](https://platform.openai.com).\n   - Set `LLM_PROVIDER=openai` and assign `LLM_API_KEY=sk-...`.\n3. **Google Calendar API**:\n   - In Google Cloud Console, enable the **Google Calendar API v3**.\n   - Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID with redirect URI `http://localhost:5000/api/calendar/callback`.\n   - Set `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, and `GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN`.\n4. **Email Provider (Nodemailer / SMTP)**:\n   - For development testing, create a free Mailtrap account or supply production SMTP credentials (`EMAIL_HOST`, `EMAIL_PORT`, `EMAIL_USER`, `EMAIL_PASSWORD`).\n\n*(Note: If any third-party credentials are not supplied, the platform automatically activates self-contained development fallback adapters with clear logging).*\n\n---\n\n## 7. Automated Test Execution & Actual Results\n\nBackend test execution runs via Jest against an isolated in-memory MongoDB server:\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\backend\nnpm test\n```\n\n### Actual Test Suite Execution Log:\n```text\nPASS tests/auth.test.ts\n  Authentication & User Profile API\n    √ should register a new user successfully (495 ms)\n    √ should reject registration with duplicate email (275 ms)\n    √ should login an existing user with correct credentials (390 ms)\n    √ should reject login with incorrect password (398 ms)\n    √ should reject unauthenticated request to /api/users/profile (93 ms)\n    √ should get and update user profile when authenticated (339 ms)\n\nPASS tests/resumes.test.ts\n  Resume Management & AI Section Generation API\n    √ should create, retrieve, update, and delete a structured resume (412 ms)\n    √ should prevent User B from accessing or updating User A resume (185 ms)\n    √ should generate resume section via AI integration (194 ms)\n\nPASS tests/chat.test.ts\n  AI Career Assistant Chat API\n    √ should create session, exchange messages, and preserve conversation history (395 ms)\n    √ should prevent User B from reading User A chat sessions (199 ms)\n\nPASS tests/bookings.test.ts\n  Consultation Booking & Concurrency Safeguards API\n    √ should reject bookings scheduled in the past (232 ms)\n    √ should successfully create a pending booking and prevent double booking of overlapping slot (140 ms)\n    √ should support server-side pagination, search, sorting, and filtering (162 ms)\n\nPASS tests/payments.test.ts\n  Stripe Payments & Webhook Idempotency API\n    √ should create a checkout session for a pending booking (420 ms)\n    √ should process webhook idempotently and transition booking to CONFIRMED (280 ms)\n\nTest Suites: 5 passed, 5 total\nTests:       16 passed, 16 total\nSnapshots:   0 total\nTime:        11.726 s\nRan all test suites.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Production Build Results\n\n### Backend Build (`npm run build` in `backend`):\n```text\n> career-platform-backend@1.0.0 build\n> tsc\nProcess exited with code 0.\n```\n\n### Frontend Build (`npm run build` in `frontend`):\n```text\n> career-platform-frontend@1.0.0 build\n> next build\n\n  ▲ Next.js 14.2.35\n\n   Creating an optimized production build ...\n ✓ Compiled successfully\n   Linting and checking validity of types ...\n   Collecting page data ...\n ✓ Generating static pages (15/15)\n   Finalizing page optimization ...\n   Collecting build traces ...\n\nRoute (app)                              Size     First Load JS\n┌ ○ /                                    3.28 kB         108 kB\n├ ○ /_not-found                          873 B          88.2 kB\n├ ○ /chat                                177 B           113 kB\n├ ƒ /chat/[sessionId]                    254 B           113 kB\n├ ○ /consultations                       3.16 kB         113 kB\n├ ○ /consultations/book                  7.66 kB         113 kB\n├ ○ /dashboard                           2.22 kB         112 kB\n├ ○ /login                               3.32 kB         134 kB\n├ ○ /payment/cancel                      5.5 kB          111 kB\n├ ○ /payment/success                     1.96 kB         112 kB\n├ ○ /profile                             6.88 kB         112 kB\n├ ○ /register                            3.4 kB          134 kB\n├ ○ /resumes                             2.2 kB          112 kB\n├ ƒ /resumes/[id]/edit                   101 kB          211 kB\n├ ƒ /resumes/[id]/preview                3.83 kB         114 kB\n└ ○ /resumes/create                      6.52 kB         112 kB\n+ First Load JS shared by all            87.3 kB\n\nProcess exited with code 0.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Known Limitations & Technical Trade-offs\n\n1. **In-Memory vs. Distributed Job Queue**: Stripe webhook delivery and subsequent calendar/email operations execute synchronously within the webhook transaction. In an ultra-high-throughput enterprise setup, scheduling calendar and email jobs through a durable queue (e.g. BullMQ / Redis) provides distributed worker retries across restarts.\n2. **ATS Compatibility**: The ATS Classic template conforms to semantic HTML, standard section hierarchies, single-column design, and raw text readability. However, because enterprise applicant tracking parsers vary widely across vendors (Workday, Taleo, Greenhouse, Lever), universal 100% parsing fidelity cannot be mathematically guaranteed across all proprietary engines.\n3. **Local Development Adapters**: When API keys are not supplied for OpenAI, Stripe, Google Calendar, or Nodemailer, development adapters return deterministic mock data with explicit log markers.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Completed Acceptance Checklist\n\n- [x] Full-stack application runs with separated frontend and backend architectures.\n- [x] MongoDB connectivity with indexes, unique constraints, and multi-tenant scoping.\n- [x] Secure registration, login, logout, and HTTP-only cookie authentication.\n- [x] User profile management with complete career metadata.\n- [x] AI career assistant supporting persistent, multi-thread conversations.\n- [x] Complete Resume CRUD with structured data storage.\n- [x] AI section generation and refinement integration.\n- [x] Both Modern Professional and ATS Classic templates implemented losslessly.\n- [x] Tiptap rich-text editor integrated with bidirectional state synchronization.\n- [x] Resume live preview, print-to-PDF, and HTML export.\n- [x] Consultant directory with real-time calculated slot availability.\n- [x] Concurrency protection preventing double-booking and past appointments.\n- [x] Stripe Checkout integration with backend-calculated pricing.\n- [x] Stripe webhook processing with raw HMAC signature verification.\n- [x] Webhook idempotency ledger tracking processed event IDs.\n- [x] Google Calendar integration adapter with meeting URL generation.\n- [x] Email confirmation notifications with failure isolation.\n- [x] Real-time dashboard analytics populated from MongoDB aggregations.\n- [x] Server-side pagination, search, sorting whitelist, and status filtering.\n- [x] OpenAPI / Swagger documentation rendered at `/api/docs`.\n- [x] All 16 automated API tests executed and passing.\n- [x] Clean TypeScript and Next.js production builds verified with zero errors."}
